course: dictionary
lesson: 3764
title: One word, many meanings: focus
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Focus has more than one meaning, so the words around it tell you which one you need. «Putting the phone in another room during homework is one of the simplest ways to focus.» The clues are phone and homework, so focus means giving all your attention to one thing.
explain: Look at the same word in a different text. «Exposure is how much light a photo lets in, and focus is which part looks sharp.» Here focus means which part is clear, not what you are thinking about. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Science uses focus too. «The eye sees light that enters through the pupil; the lens focuses it at the back of the eye.» Here focus is a verb meaning to adjust something so the picture comes out clear and sharp.
fact: To focus can mean to give all your attention to one thing.
fact: The focus is the main thing people are paying attention to.
fact: «In focus» means clear and sharp; «out of focus» means blurry.
fact: In science, the focus of a lens is the point where rays of light meet after passing through it.
fact: Staying focused is easier with sleep, food and few distractions. A magnifying glass can focus sunlight into a spot hot enough to start a fire, so never aim one at paper or people.
exercise: «Putting the phone in another room during homework is one of the simplest ways to focus.» What does focus mean here? | To take a photo | To switch the lights off | To run very fast | *To give all your attention to one thing
exercise: A photo that is «out of focus» looks how? | Full of colour | Bright and sharp | Very large | *Blurry
exercise: In science, what is the focus of a lens? | The biggest hole in the lens | The noise a lens makes | *The point where rays of light meet after passing through it | The part of the lens you hold in your hand
test: «Looking at something far away lets the focusing muscles of the eyes relax.» In this sentence, focusing means what? | Closing the eyes tightly | Running after something | Looking for a friend | *Adjusting the eyes so they see clearly
test: Which word means the main thing people are paying attention to? | blur | lens | pupil | *focus
exam: A magnifying glass can focus sunlight into a spot hot enough to start a fire. What does focus mean here? | To make the sun go away | To cool the air down | *To bring sunlight rays together into one hot spot | To paint the glass
